  "facts": [
    "The Raftsund Bridge, a 711‑metre cantilever road bridge, opened on 6 November 1998, costing 125 million kr and marking the final link of the long Vesterålen bridges.",
    "With a 298‑metre main span and 45‑metre clearance below, the Raftsund Bridge carries the E10 highway across the Raftsundet strait, connecting Austvågøya and Hinnøya.",
    "As part of the Lofast project, the Raftsund Bridge helped complete the mainland‑to‑Lofoten road network in December 2007, transforming regional travel."
